messages:
sana: Heads-up  i'm landing a small quickstart cleanup focused on auth hygiene and deploy clarifications. PR: github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4520. Changes: replace an inline long-lived key example with guidance on token rotation, add a compact Rust snippet for the quickstart (we've had a few users ask), normalize REDWOOD_API_KEY across examples, and fix a broken internal anchor.

omar: Nice. can you paste the rust snippet you added? want to make sure the import/constructor lines match what the SDK team shipped.

sana: sure  kept it intentionally tiny and sync-friendly:
```rust
use redwood_inference::Redwood;
use std::env;

fn main() {
    let api_key = env::var("REDWOOD_API_KEY").expect("set REDWOOD_API_KEY");
    let client = Redwood::new(&api_key);
    let resp = client.generate("gpt-rt-1", "Hello from Quickstart").unwrap();
    println!("{}", resp.text);
}
```

lucy: I like the Rust example. please also add a one-paragraph note about short-lived tokens and point to /guides/security#token-rotation. we've seen users accidentally paste long-lived keys into examples.

sana: good call  added a short banner under "Auth": "Prefer short-lived or rotated keys; use secrets managers. See /guides/security#token-rotation for rotation patterns." and swapped every occurrence of `REDSYS_TOKEN` -> `REDWOOD_API_KEY` in code samples and docker-compose.

omar: did you also update the docker run and github actions examples to read from envs/secrets rather than inline values? that's where people tend to copy sensitive data.

sana: yes  changed docker examples to `docker run -e REDWOOD_API_KEY="$REDWOOD_API_KEY" redwood/hello:latest` and replaced the demo github action step with `secrets.REDWOOD_API_KEY`. left a commented line showing use of a secrets manager action.

lucy: small ask  add a 2-line migration note for node/python SDK changes (ctor vs setApiKey) and link to /sdk/migrate so folks upgrading old tutorials won't be surprised.

sana: added Migration notes with two examples (node and python) and the /sdk/migrate link. also corrected a stale anchor that was pointing at `/guides/auth#old-token-guidance`  now points to `/guides/security#token-rotation`.

docs-bot: ci:docs  linkcheck + lint passed for PR #4520 :white_check_mark:

omar: i'll take a quick review pass and run the single-file + docker deploy locally. if green i'll approve. one tiny nit: in the Rust snippet prefer `response.text` fallback handling in case of different response shapes; i'll push that if needed.

sana: thanks! i'm happy to take that commit. will merge once you approve and CI stays green. tagging docs-bot for staging publish after merge.

docs-bot: publish:docs scheduled  staging will pick up the change in ~10m after merge.
